    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d306">

                <pb facs="0851" n="822" xml:id="pg822"/>

                <head>306. Telegram From the Department of State to
                        the Embassy in Pakistan<anchor n="1"
                        xml:id="d306-f1"/>
                </head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>Washington</placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1971-12-14T21:36:00+00:00">December 14, 1971,
                        2136Z</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>224704. If and when Bangla Desh and or Indian forces occupy Dacca, you should not
                    take any initiative to establish or encourage contact with them beyond that
                    which may be required in emergency situations to protect American lives or to
                    otherwise assure safety of your mission.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#bold">Rogers</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d306-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d306-f1-content">
                <p>Source: National Archives, RG 59, Central Files 1970–73, POL 27 INDIA–PAK. Secret; Priority;
                        Exdis. Drafted by U. Alexis Johnson, cleared in the White House
                    by Saunders, and approved by Johnson. Repeated to New Delhi and
                    Calcutta.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
